Subject: compute entry size with sizeof instead of null-pointer arithmetic

ext4_xattr_list() sized its buffer with the old
(char *)((T *)0 + 1) - (char *)(T *)0 idiom. That is undefined behaviour, and
UBSan flags it on every call:

    ext4_xattr.c:906:51: runtime error: applying non-zero offset 32 to null pointer

sizeof is exactly equivalent and well-defined. Worth fixing not because the
generated code is wrong today, but because the noise buries genuine findings on
a sanitizer run -- which is how the xattr-remove NULL dereference fixed in the
previous patch was found.

--- a/src/ext4_xattr.c
+++ b/src/ext4_xattr.c
@@ -899,13 +899,8 @@
 					    *)(list->name + name_len + 1);
 			}
 
-			/*
-			 * Size calculation by pointer arithmetics.
-			 */
-			buf_len +=
-			    (char *)((struct ext4_xattr_list_entry *)0 + 1) +
-			    name_len + 1 -
-			    (char *)(struct ext4_xattr_list_entry *)0;
+			buf_len += sizeof(struct ext4_xattr_list_entry) +
+				   name_len + 1;
 		}
 	}
 
